        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castlebay, Barra, Outer Hebrides, Scotland\n- Organizations: Castlebay community council area\n- Buildings: Kisimul Castle, Kiessimul Castle\n- Concepts: Scottish Gaelic names\n\nFacts:\n- Castlebay is the main village on the island of Barra in the Outer Hebrides, Scotland.\n- Castlebay is also a community council area on Barra in the Outer Hebrides, Scotland.\n- The Scottish Gaelic name for Castlebay is \"Bàgh a' Chaisteil.\"\n- Kisimul Castle is also known as Kiessimul Castle.\n- Kisimul Castle is a small medieval castle on a small island off Castlebay, Barra, in the Outer Hebrides, Scotland.\n- The Scottish Gaelic name for Kisimul Castle is \"Caisteal Chiosmuil.\"",
